%% Discovery skips nothing (TGLP modules.tex, Compilation, first step: "the
%% compiler collects every .glp file of the program's directory tree"), so
%% boot_direct.glp, mad_boot.glp and mad_boot/play.glp are modules of this
%% program like any other, and each is type-checked against its scope (second
%% step).  Each defines stray/1 with no declaration, so the program is refused
%% naming all three.  Until 2026-10-03 discovery left the three out by their
%% names and the program loaded, run(X) giving 1.
exported procedure run(Integer).
run(1).
